    [McpServerTool(Name = "yuki_sales_process_sales_invoices", ReadOnly = false, Destructive = true, Idempotent = false, OpenWorld = true)]
    [Description("This call is meant to make an electronic connection with Yuki in order to import sales invoices from a webshop or ERP system into a Yuki administration. This webservice is specifically developed for this matter and serves as an alternative to manually input sales invoices within the Yuki web application. Procedure Make sure the administration in the Yuki domain is correctly set up. In order to use the sales webservice a few conditions should be set in the domain: The domain has an active Trial, Small, Medium, Large or Unlimited bundle OR If the domain has a Minimal bundle, ask the accountant to activate Yuki Sales Webservice at the Accountancy features. Does the entrepreneur wants to link invoices to a Project or wants to use the payment method Direct Debit; then this functionality is available in a Medium bundle or higher. Create the XML with sales invoices Collect all the invoice details in an XML file and submit it to our web service. The web service will validate the XML file according to the XML schema (XSD) . In case the XML file is not validated by the web service, the process will be cancelled and the web service will send a detailed validation notification. Validation If the validation process is successfully completed, the invoices will be extracted from the XML file and processed one by one in your administration. During the processing of an invoice, new contact persons (customers) and products will be automatically created. Existing contact persons will be matched by means of a reference or name and address details. Existing products will be matched by their description. In case the product details differ from the saved details such as price, VAT percentage or ledger account number, the new details found in the current invoice will be recorded. Process The process will be cancelled for incomplete or incorrect invoices by which all actions will be undone such as the creation of new contact persons or products. An invoice can be marked as incomplete when new products are offered without prices or VAT percentages or when new contact persons are provided without address details. A complete and correct invoice can be sent by email to the customer after it is processed automatically or sent over the Peppol network. In case an existing invoice lay out is recorded in the XML file, the respective lay out will be used. Response At the end of the ProcessSalesInvoices process, this web service creates a response XML document in which the processing status of the invoices and possible validation notifications are recorded. This XML document is specified in an XML schema (XSD) and can be processed by your application if desired. /www.yukiworks.be/schemas/SalesInvoicesResponse.xsd Note: when a batch with invoices includes incorrect invoices, after 6 incorrect invoices the webservice is automatically stopped. Functional description Below you can find a description of the fields. The XML schema also includes a description of the fields as well as which values and datatypes are expected. SalesInvoice: Reference In this field you can record the invoice number. Invoice has been created, printed and/or sent externally. Consequently the invoice number has been provided externally. The field 'Reference' includes the invoice number and the field 'Process' has to have value 'True' so that Yuki is aware that the invoice and its corresponding details can be processed. Invoice has to be processed, printed and/ or sent manually by Yuki. Therefore the invoice number will be provided by Yuki. The field 'Reference' has to be left blank and the field 'Process' has to have value 'False'. SalesInvoice: PaymentMethod In this field you can record the payment method of the invoice. Possible options: Unspecified (the payment method of the invoice will be 'Bank transfer' in Yuki) ElectronicTransfer (Bank transfer) DirectCollection ( minimum Medium bundle needed) CreditCard DebitCard Cash iDeal Online ToSettle (Credit Sales Invoices) SalesInvoice: PaymentID Here you can add the structured payment reference or a free text payment reference which your customer can use when making the transfer. Based on the PaymentID Yuki can automatically match the invoice with the bank transaction&gt; SalesInvoice: PurchaseOrderNumber If your customer requests a Purchase order number, you can add this here. SalesInvoice: SourceInvoiceReference You can add up to three references if you have to refer in this invoice to previous documents. SalesInvoice: Buyer Reference In this field you can add a buyer reference the refer to your customer. Salesinvoice: InvoicePeriod Underneath this section you can add a start date and an end date to refer to the period the invoice is created for. SalesInvoice: Process In this field you indicate whether or not you want the invoices to be processed immediately. To process the invoice, you need to enter the correct invoice number in the field 'Reference'. If the value is 'True', the invoice will be processed without consent in Yuki and sent to the customer (if indicated). If the value is 'False', the invoice will be directed to the list 'Ready to be sent' and the invoice has to be approved before it can be processed. ATTENTION: 1. The option 'process' 'false' cannot be used for a Minimal bundle. 2. If the TAG Process is missing, Yuki will assume the value 'False'. SalesInvoice: EmailToCustomer If you choose to process an invoice, you can indicate in this field whether or not you want the invoice to be sent by email directly to the customer. This function needs to be enabled first in the sales settings. ATTENTION The option 'EmailtoCustomer' 'true' cannot be used for a Minimal bundle. In case you do not want the invoice to be sent, you leave this field blank of enter the value 'False'. SalesInvoice: SentToPeppol Important: At the time of release, this feature is only available for Yuki Bundel owners. The accountancyfeature 'Yuki Sales Webservice' is not enough to use the Peppol functionality. The invoice can be sent immediately over the Peppol network to your customer. Your Yuki administration should be registered through Yuki to allow sending invoices over the Peppol network (you can check this in the settings of your domain). Make sure you provide the CoC or VAT number and address details of your customer. The element 'Process' should always be set as 'true'. If the customer's VAT or CoC number cannot be found on the Peppol network, the webservice will return an error message. SalesInvoice: Lay-out In this field you can choose the desired invoice lay-out. If you leave this field blank, the default invoice lay-out will be selected. SalesInvoice: Notes If you need to add some additional information regarding the invoice or a general message, this can be added into the Note field&gt; SalesInvoice: Date The invoice date SalesInvoice: DueDate The due date SalesInvoice: PriceList In this field you can choose the desired price list. If you leave this field blank, the default price list will be selected. If you offer a combination of prices inclusive and exclusive of VAT, it is useful to select either a price list inclusive or exclusive of VAT. In the event that the price is inclusive of VAT, it will be recorded well on the invoice. However, if the item is saved in a price list exclusive of VAT and you create an invoice with the same item in the Yuki Sales functionality, the price will be considered as exclusive of VAT and will be calculated and recorded accordingly on the invoice. ATTENTION The prices, VAT rates and revenue accounts that are recorded have priority. SalesInvoice: Currency The currency of the sales invoice. If you leave this field blank, the default currency 'EUR' will be selected. If no price list is recorded, the default price list will be selected. If this list is not set in a foreign currency, you will receive the following notification: 'The pricelist's currency \"EUR\" does not match with the invoice's'. If the currency differs from the foreign currency in the price list, you will receive the following notification: ' The pricelist's currency \"USD\" does not match with the invoice's'. If you leave the field 'Currency' blank but select a price list in a foreign currency, you will receive the following notification: 'The pricelist's currency \"USD\" does not match with the invoice's'. SalesInvoice: ProjectID In this field you can enter the ID of the project to which you want link the document. Recording this parameter makes the parameter 'ProjectCode' irrelevant. Medium bundle or higher has to be enabled in order to use this functionality. SalesInvoice: ProjectCode In this field you can enter the code of the project to which you want to link the document. This parameter is only relevant if the parameter 'ProjectID' is not given. Medium bundle or higher has to be enabled in order to use this functionality. Salesinvoice: Remarks The entered information will not be recorded on the invoice but saved as a remark and attached to the sales invoice. SalesInvoice: DocumentFileName When you want to send the pdf along, you can add the pdf name in this field. SalesInvoice: DocumentBase64 When adding the pdf, you can add in this field the pdf as a Base64 string. Yuki will visualize the Base64 string into the actual PDF document. Contact: Contact In the Contact fields the contact/customer of the invoice will be recorded. Yuki will first look for an existing contact in the Address book. Yuki will search for: Contact code in the field 'ContactCode' (in case one is recorded). Full name in the field 'FullName' (in case contact code is not found or recorded) Yuki will create a new contact if an existing contact is not found. Contact: found by ContactCode (on the contact card) If a contact code is used, the address details of an existing contact will always be overwritten by the current value in the XML source file. To avoid a field being overwritten, the element can be removed from the XML source file HINT : if you are using customer IDs or customer codes in your application, send them also within the xml. Therefore you will always have a one-on-one match between the customer and the invoice in both applications. Contact: found by FullName (name or company name on the contact card) If a contact is found with the same name, only the fields that are left blank for that contact will be completed with data from the XML source file. For the address details applies the same rule that details will only be completed if they match the existing details. Eg. Address 'Dorpstraat 40, Ons Dorp' will be completed with 'Dorpstraat 40, 1234 XX , Ons Dorp' in case the address and city are the same and the postal code is also recorded in the XML file. Contact: Addressline When using a peppol integration, it is important to use AddresslineAddressLine_1 and not leave this empty. Leaving this empty and only using AddresslineAddressLine_2, will result in an error. Contact: EmailAddress You can only enter one email address. This address will be saved in the contact card of the customer and will be recorded as type 'Invoice'. If this address changes, it can be recorded with a new invoice through the web service. The old address will be set to type 'Other' and the new address will receive the type 'Invoice'. **Contact: OIN **When sending your invoice over the Peppol network, you can use also the OIN number (Organization Identifiication number) as your contact's Peppol identifier (NL contacts only). **Contact: GLN **When sending your invoice over the Peppol network, you can use also the GLN number (Global location number) as your contact's Peppol identifier Contact: ContactType You can define if a customer is a private Person or a Company. Contact: BankAccount In case a bank account is recorded, this bank account will be saved in the contact card of the customer. The account number will also be used as account number for this invoice. Thus, it is possible that multiple account numbers are recorded for one customer. Contact: BIC In case a BIC code is recorded, this code along with the account number will be saved in the contact card of the customer. The account number and BIC code will also be used as account number for this invoice. ATTENTION It is also possible to create foreign bank accounts. InvoiceLine: Description The description of the invoice line. If this field is left blank or not shown, the description of the field 'ProductDescription' is used. InvoiceLine: Remarks This is an extra description that can be recorded for each invoice line. The text will be placed as a new line aligned underneath the current invoice line. HINT Een newline is created with the code InvoiceLine: ProductQuantity The quantity of the sales item described in the invoice line. InvoiceLine: LineAmount This decimal field sets the amount of the invoice line. It can be used to override calculation of the line amount based on quantity and price per article. This amount is VAT inclusive when the VATIncluded node is set to true for the InvoiceLine Product and VAT exclusive when the node is set to false. BEWARE: It is not preferred to supply this field but rather use the calculation based on the quantity and item price. ATTENTION We do not recommend to use this field. It differs from the calculation methods of Yuki! InvoiceLine: LineVATAmount This decimal field sets the VAT amount of the invoice line. It can be used to override calculation of the line VAT amount based on the line amount and vat percentage used. BEWARE: It is not preferred to supply this field but rather use the calculation based on the amount and vat percentage. ATTENTIONWe do not recommend to use this field. It differs from the calculation methods of Yuki! Product: Description The description of a sales item with a maximum length of 60 characters. Longer descriptions will be shortened. This description has to be unique. If the sales item cannot be found in Yuki, a new sales item will be created by means of the details found in the XML source file. If the field 'InvoiceLine:Description' is left blank, the field 'Product:Description' will be printed on the invoice. Product: Reference The reference of a sales item with a maximum length of 40 characters. Longer references will be shortened. This reference has to be unique. Product: Category This field can be used in the future to allocate categories. Currently only the values 'NULL' and '13' are allowed (13 = category sales items). This field is mandatory. Product: SalesPrice The sales price of a sales item. If the sales items is already created and can be found by means of the description/reference, this field can be left blank or be recorded with a 0-value. Yuki will only use the data from the XML file if the fields 'SalesPrice', 'VATType' and 'VATPercentage' are recorded, . Otherwise, the information will be copied from the price list. If one of the three elements are missing, the sales item can always be found in the price list. This information is necessary in order to record the item on the invoice. Therefore, a sales item cannot be created in the price list without this information. Product: VATPercentage The VAT percentage of a sales item. This field is used in combination with the field 'VATType' in order to calculate the VAT rate. If the VAT rate does not exist, the invoice cannot be created. Product: VATIncluded In this field you indicate whether or not the sales price is inclusive of VAT. This field is used in combination with the fields 'SalesPrice' and 'VATType' in order to calculate the VAT amount and sales price. By default, the value will be set to 'False' if this field is left blank in combination with the sales price. Value 'False' = sales price exclusive of VAT. Value 'True' = sales price inclusive of VAT. Product: VATType In this field you can select the VAT type of a sales item. This field is used in combination with the fields 'SalesPrice' and 'VATType' in order to calculate the VAT amount and sales price. Possible combinations of VAT percentage and VAT rates are: VAT Type Percentage Description 0 0% Exempted from VAT 1 Variable VAT high 2 Variable VAT low 4 0% VAT 0% 6 0% Export outside EU 7 0% Export inside EU 8 Country specific VAT installation and distance sales inside the EU 17 0% VAT reverse charged 19 0% Export of goods inside EU (purchases 2010) 20 0% Export of services inside EU (services 2010) 21 12% VAT on mid-rate (only in Belgium) 40 Variable VAT digital services and/or distance selling (OSS) VATDescription: Remarks This field can be used in combination with 'VATType 8'. This is not mandatory. The VATDescription of each type can be found in the VAT settings of your domain. Product: GLAccountCode The code of the ledger accounts in Yuki: If the sales item is not yet registered in Yuki and this field is left blank or contains an invalid value (inactive ledger account number is also invalid), the default ledger account with code '80000 sales and services rendered (NL)' or '700000 Revenue (BE) will be used. If the sales item is already registered in Yuki and this field is left blank, the ledger account that is linked to the sales item in Yuki will be used. If the sales item is already registered in Yuki and this field contains a valid value, the ledger account that matches the value of the GLAccountCode will be used. Moreover the ledger account number that is linked to the existing sales item will not be adjusted. Product: Remarks This remark will be added to the sales item in Yuki and will not be shown on the invoice AccrualDate When the revenue of an article should be divided equally over different periods., you can use the accrual option. The AccrualDate is the start that when Yuki should start to accrue revenue. If left empty, the invoice date is used. AccrualPeriods The number of periods over which to accrue the invoice revenue. AccrualInterval The number of month for each accrual period. Default value is 1. This call creates or changes data in Yuki.")]
    public static async System.Threading.Tasks.Task<string> ProcessSalesInvoices(
        YukiSessionManager sessionManager,
        SalesSoapClient client,
        string administrationId,
        [Description("a well-formed XML document (as a string), per the Yuki XSD for this call")] string xmlDoc)
    {
        var result = await sessionManager.ExecuteAsync(sessionId => client.ProcessSalesInvoicesAsync(sessionId, administrationId, YukiXml.Parse(xmlDoc, nameof(xmlDoc))));
        return YukiResult.Format(result);
    }

